#====================================================================
# E247 — Static C API archive omits its C++ runtime from pkg-config
#====================================================================

id:                     E247
trigger_tool:           pkg-config|clang|ld|conan_test
phase:                  linking
error_signature:        undefined symbol: std::__n1|undefined symbol: operator new|undefined symbol: __cxa_begin_catch

severity:               2
category:               linking|pkg-config|static-library|consumer-contract
match_keywords:         Libs.private, pkg-config --static, C API, C++ objects, libc++, operator new, std::__n1
title:                  Static C API archive omits its C++ runtime from pkg-config metadata

root_cause:             A static archive contains C++ implementation objects behind a C API, but its installed pkg-config Libs.private field omits the C++ runtime, so pure C consumers use the C linker without required ABI libraries.
affected_scope:         C/C++ libraries that expose a C API, compile C++ objects into a static archive, and install pkg-config metadata for downstream C consumers.
verification_cmd:       pkg-config --static --libs ${PACKAGE} && build and run an unchanged pure C consumer

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           propagate-static-cxx-runtime-in-pkg-config
rec_description:        Add the selected C++ runtime and other private system libraries to the installed .pc Libs.private field for static packages, while keeping Conan cpp_info.system_libs consistent.
rec_command:            validate pkg-config --static output, then compile and run a C consumer without manual C++ flags
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               package-metadata-fix

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      configure-upstream-pkg-config-generation
fallback_description:   If the upstream build exposes a supported input for private pkg-config libraries, pass the selected C++ runtime there so the generated build-tree and installed metadata agree without package-time rewriting.
fallback_command:       configure the upstream private-library list and verify the generated .pc before installation
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          build-system-metadata-fix

forbid_1_pattern:       LINKER_LANGUAGE CXX|rename .*\.c .*\.cpp|manual .*\-lc\+\+
forbid_1_reason:        Changing the consumer linker language or injecting flags only in the test masks the installed package metadata defect.
forbid_1_consequence:   Real C pkg-config consumers continue to fail even though the package test passes.
forbid_2_pattern:       cpp_info\.system_libs.*only|Conan metadata only
forbid_2_reason:        Conan-generated metadata does not repair an upstream pkg-config file installed by the package.
forbid_2_consequence:   Conan CMake consumers may pass while direct pkg-config consumers still fail.

principles:

causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

